{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa in Cooking School: Italian Food", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Italian Food Traditions", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Delicious Food > Italy", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations about advice for a healthy lifestyle.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Count and Non-Count Nouns", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Count nouns are things we can count.<br /><br /><ul><li>They can be singular or plural (a casserole, two casseroles).  </li> <li>You can use <span class=\"strong\">some </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">any </span>  with count nouns.</li> <span class=\"italic\">       \tExample: some recipes</span>  <li>You can also use <span class=\"strong\">a few </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">many</span> .</li> <span class=\"italic\">       \tExample: a few teaspoons </span>  <li>When a count noun is singular, we must use a word like <span class=\"italic\">a/the/my/this</span>.</li>        \t<span class=\"italic\">Example: I am making a casserole.</span>  <li>When a countable noun is plural, we can use it alone.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: I love casseroles.</span> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Non-count nouns are things that we cannot divide into separate things.  They are materials, substances or amounts.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>They are usually considered singular. You never put an <span class=\"italic\">s</span> at the end.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: I added lobster and salmon to the pasta.</span>  <li>You can use <span class=\"strong\">some </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">any </span>  with non-count nouns.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: some butter </span>  <li>We can use <span class=\"strong\">a little </span>  and <span class=\"strong\">much </span>  with non-count nouns.</li> <span class=\"italic\">Example: a little garlic</span> </ul>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to prepare ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make food", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I prepared seafood pasta last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about preparing meals, such as for family traditions.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "entire ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "whole; complete ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I made enough food for the entire neighborhood!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "instead   ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in the place of", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I prepared a seafood casserole instead.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "seafood  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a variety of species that live in the ocean, like lobster ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love seafood macaroni and cheese.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lobster ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a large, red type of seafood ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Lobster is my favorite type of seafood.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "feast ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a very large meal ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your meal was a real feast!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "casserole ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a meal with meat and vegetables cooked together ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I made a seafood casserole last night.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "butter ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a product made from milk, often used in cooking ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love cooking with butter.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "celery  ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a long, thin light green vegetable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Then, I added celery to the casserole.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"content": "engenn4le04ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Talk to friends or classmates from different countries, or search for information on the Internet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find information about 4 different cooking traditions in 4 different countries. What is the special occasion? What do people eat? How do they prepare food?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write sentences about the traditions. You can start with <span class=\"italic\">\u201cIn Thailand ...\u201d</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Practice reading the sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share the information with a partner or the class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I ask and research about cooking traditions in different countries.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write complete statements about cooking.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share the information with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn4le04ob06re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "50", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  So, how did your original recipe for satay chicken sticks go last night?<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Logan</span>: It was great! My girlfriend wants to visit Thailand to try the real thing. How was the seafood macaroni and cheese?"}, {"image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "14000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Actually, I changed recipes. I prepared a seafood casserole instead. I bought the salmon from a local fisherman to make sure it was very fresh. I cooked it with butter and garlic. Then I started adding many things, like lobster, celery and broccoli."}, {"image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img02.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "36000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Logan</span> : So your meal was a real feast!<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Yes, you could say that! I made enough food for the entire neighborhood!"}, {"image": "engenn4le04ob06re2img02.jpg", "id": 4, "time": "45500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Logan</span>: In my family, we often make casseroles to celebrate special occasions. Each member of the family has their favorite casserole.<br />\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>:  That's a nice family tradition."}], "coverimg": "engenn4le04ob06re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "I can talk about food and customs.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express a goal or a purpose.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express general quantities.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What special traditions does your family have?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What foods do you prepare? ", "type": "Fre